<title>UK: BT would attempt to challenge windfall tax.</title>
<headline>BT would attempt to challenge windfall tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sir Iain Vallance, the chairman of British Telecommunications Plc, said on Thursday that the company owed it to its shareholders to try to challenge legally any windfall tax on its profits imposed by the new Labour government.</p>
<p>&quot;If we are stung in a big way for this tax and if it can be challenged legally, we owe it to our shareholders to challenge it,&quot; Vallance told BBC radio.</p>
<p>But he added that the company would be &quot;very sad&quot; to start a partnership with Labour on such a footing.</p>
</text>
